{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfry2k2EGfuQtYBoLMxTg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `AgeFallback` enum and the exact-pin skip are in place. The two requested test files pass (67 tests), and the neighbouring resolver tests pass too (104 across four files). I did not commit.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`src/fromager/resolver.py`**\n  - New `AgeFallback` enum (`ALL`, `NEWEST`, `NONE`). Module-level, so it is importable as `fromager.resolver.AgeFallback`.\n  - `find_all_matching_from_provider()` takes `age_fallback: AgeFallback = AgeFallback.ALL` in place of the boolean. Its docstring describes the pin skip and the enum.\n  - If the provider's constraint for `req.name` is a single `==` pin, age filtering is skipped and the INFO message is logged. The existing `_has_equality_pin()` helper does the check, so wildcard pins like `==1.*` still get age-filtered.\n  - The filtering moved into a private `_filter_by_age()` helper that applies the three fallback behaviours and their exact log messages.\n- **`src/fromager/bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`**: multi-version mode passes `AgeFallback.NEWEST`, single-version passes `AgeFallback.ALL`. I updated the `multiple_versions` and `cache_wheel_server_url` docstrings to match.\n- **Tests**\n  - `tests/test_cooldown.py`: the old `fallback_on_empty_age_filter=False` test now uses `AgeFallback.NONE`. New cases cover NEWEST, the default, an exact pin skipping the filter, a pinned version outside the window not triggering the warning, range constraints still being filtered, and a wildcard pin not counting as a pin.\n  - `tests/test_bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`: a parametrized test checks the `age_fallback` value per mode. Two end-to-end cases use a mocked PyPI index with two releases from 2024 and a 2026 cutoff. Multi-version builds only the newest release, single-version keeps both, and an exact pin to an old release resolves.\n\n**Things to know**\n\n- **Cache-server fallback is now effectively dead code.** `find_matches()` raises when no candidates remain, so `_resolve_and_extend()` never sees an empty list from the age filter. I kept the fallback code and only corrected its docstrings, since the spec didn't ask for removal. Say if you want it removed.\n- **Lint and types:** `ruff format` and `ruff check` are clean on the four files I touched. `hatch run mypy:check` on the two source files reports two errors, at `resolver.py:1233` and `:1356`. Both are in the GitHub/GitLab tag-provider pagination code, which I did not change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10968,"cache_read_input_tokens":139778,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10968},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f96719f9-1d6c-4521-afff-e32c36e25008","uuid":"93a0c340-e284-4686-b77b-24e695381003","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:19:24.612Z","request_id":"req_011Cfry2jiNpSqBNuo2FesD2"}
